  "_comment": "Garmin pass 2026-09-12 — the catalog had five inReach rows and no Garmin watch or handheld; a list in the candidate scan typed fēnix 7 Pro and fēnix 8 Pro Sapphire and inReach Mini 3 Plus. Every row is the maker's own Specs table, read per SKU from garmin.com (each source_url is the SKU's own /pn/ page). A watch's figure is Garmin's headline weight — with the included band; the case-only figure stays in the quote — and where Garmin prints a with-band figure in parentheses (Venu, vívoactive) that is the one stored, since it is what is worn. fēnix 8 AMOLED pages print one spec table for the steel and titanium versions, so the two are separate rows by material; the Solar, Pro and Sapphire editions come only in titanium and say nothing. Editions that weigh exactly what their base row weighs (Tactical, Music, inReach-equipped fēnix 9 Pro, tactix Elite, the Mini 2 Marine bundle) are not repeated. The fēnix 7 family is what garmin.com still lists: the 7 Pro's Solar Edition survives only as the No Wi-Fi SKU, cited at the same 79 g. Handhelds store Garmin's with-batteries figure. Three existing inReach rows (Mini 2, Mini 3, Messenger Plus) are re-cited to the maker in their own files in the same PR.",
